-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- originally rev_1787612377773650113.sql
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Frost Mage rework - talent tree content, new-C++ pass, Cluster B (docs/frost-mage-talent-tree-content-handoff.md
-- "Next up: Step 3 game plan", Cluster B - the 5 rows with a done base and an open capstone):
-- Ice Shards (73), Arctic Winds (1738), Arctic Reach (741), Frost Channeling (66), Chilled to the
-- Bone (1856), plus two bugs found and fixed along the way.
--
-- Ice Shards capstone (rank 3 only, EFFECT_1): "+6% dmg against frozen targets" - a rank-3-only
-- SPELL_AURA_DUMMY (icon 1236) read by a new check in Unit::SpellPctDamageModsDone, same
-- three-way frozen check (real freeze / Fingers of Frost / Shattering Cold) as Frostbite's Mastery
-- capstone right above it in that function (same commit as this file - see the Unit.cpp diff).
--
-- Arctic Winds capstone (rank 3 only, EFFECT_2): "Glacial Spike shatters on impact, striking up to
-- 5 additional enemies within 8 yards." Rank-3-only SPELL_AURA_DUMMY (icon 2131) checked from
-- spell_mage_glacial_spike::ConsumeIciclesAndFrostCharge (spell_mage.cpp), which finds up to 5
-- nearby enemies and casts a new dedicated damage spell (200014 "Icy Shatter" - mirrors Glacial
-- Spike's own 1500 base + 1.2 SP coeff exactly) at each, rather than re-triggering Glacial Spike
-- itself (which would re-run icicle/Fingers-of-Frost consumption per additional target).
--
-- Arctic Reach capstone (rank 2 only, EFFECT_2): "Frost damage +up to 10% based on target
-- distance, full at 30 yards." Not a stock aura type - a rank-2-only SPELL_AURA_DUMMY (icon 154)
-- gates a plain GetDistance()-based linear ramp in Unit::SpellPctDamageModsDone.
--
-- Frost Channeling capstone (rank 3 only, EFFECT_2): "Killing an enemy that yields XP/honor with
-- Frost damage restores 12% mana." A rank-3-only SPELL_AURA_DUMMY (icon 15) read from a new check
-- in Unit::Kill, using Player::isHonorOrXPTarget() (covers both the PvE and PvP cases in one call)
-- and the spellProto parameter Kill() already receives from DealDamage but wasn't using.
--
-- Chilled to the Bone: base slow effect widened to also reach Frozen Orb (spec: "Frostbolt, Cone
-- of Cold and Frozen Orb" - previously only the first two, since Frozen Orb's pulse has no
-- SpellFamilyFlags a classmask-scoped SpellMod could ever match). Fixed via a live effect-value
-- boost in spell_mage_frozen_orb_pulse (reads the mage's own ADD_FLAT_MODIFIER amount at icon 2965
-- EFFECT_1 and folds it into the pulse's slow before it applies) rather than a classmask trick.
-- Capstone (rank 3 only, EFFECT_2): "Frostbolt/Ice Lance vs monsters reduce Frozen Orb's cooldown
-- by 1 sec, Blizzard by 1 sec per 3 ticks" - a new spell_mage_chilled_to_the_bone AuraScript
-- (native ProcTypeMask widened to 327680 = direct spell damage | periodic, so both Frostbolt/Ice
-- Lance's direct hits and Blizzard's ticks reach it) using Player::ModifySpellCooldown.
--
-- Bug found and fixed along the way (docs/frost-mage-implementation-plan.md's "Damage attribution"
-- note): Frozen Orb's pulse damage/threat/combat-log currently isn't actually attributed to the
-- owning player at all (traced all the way through AuraEffect::HandlePeriodicTriggerSpellAuraTick -
-- rearchitecting that is out of scope and risks the already-working orb behavior, so flagged in
-- code rather than fixed; npc_mage_frozen_orb::GetOwnerGUID() added instead so scripts that only
-- need to look up the owning player, like the Chilled to the Bone fix above, can do so directly).
--
-- Bug found and fixed (unrelated to Cluster B, discovered while auditing spell_script_names for
-- Chilled to the Bone and Frostbite): spell_mage_biting_cold (Biting Cold's rank-3 capstone proc,
-- landed two passes ago) was written and registered in C++ but never actually bound to spell 200012
-- via spell_script_names, so it has never fired. Bound here.
--
-- Frostbite's own spell_mage_frostbite script (added in this session's earlier Frostbite pass) had
-- the same gap - also bound here for the first time.

DELETE FROM `spell_dbc` WHERE `ID` IN (15047, 16758, 12519, 31676, 44566, 44567, 44568, 200014);
