-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- originally rev_1787741473400683042.sql
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Three more bugs found via live playtest (docs/frost-mage-playtest-script.md):
--
-- 1. Conjure Refreshment (42955) kept rank 1's original learn level (75, `BaseLevel`/`SpellLevel`
--    in spell_dbc, `ReqLevel` in trainer_spell) from the single-rank bootstrap - see
--    apps/dbc-tools/source/spells/mage.csv's notes on this row. Conjure Refreshment replaces
--    Conjure Food/Water (docs/frost-mage-redesign.md sec 2, "Conjure Food / Water: This will be
--    replaced in favor of Conjure Refreshment"), which were learnable in the level 8-20 range, so
--    gating the replacement behind level 75 leaves mages without any self-sustain food/water spell
--    for most of leveling. Dropped to level 10 (both the spell itself and the one trainer_spell row
--    that teaches it - confirmed via live DB only TrainerId 16 has a row for this spell).
UPDATE `spell_dbc` SET `BaseLevel` = 10, `SpellLevel` = 10 WHERE `ID` = 42955 AND `BaseLevel` = 75 AND `SpellLevel` = 75;
UPDATE `trainer_spell` SET `ReqLevel` = 10 WHERE `SpellId` = 42955 AND `ReqLevel` = 75;

-- 2. Frozen Orb's projectile creature (npc_mage_frozen_orb, 300001 - spell_mage.cpp) was given
--    UNIT_FLAG_IMMUNE_TO_PC | UNIT_FLAG_IMMUNE_TO_NPC (0x100 | 0x200) alongside UNIT_FLAG_NOT_
--    SELECTABLE (0x2000000), evidently meant to keep the trigger from being targeted/attacked by
--    anything. That backfires: Unit::_IsValidAttackTarget (Unit.cpp) treats a caster's own
--    IsImmuneToNPC()/IsImmuneToPC() as blocking *outgoing* attacks too, not just incoming ones -
--    `(!target->HasUnitFlag(UNIT_FLAG_PLAYER_CONTROLLED) && IsImmuneToNPC())` and
--    `(target->HasUnitFlag(UNIT_FLAG_PLAYER_CONTROLLED) && IsImmuneToPC())` both key off `this`
--    (the attacker, i.e. the orb) being immune - so the orb could never register a valid attack
--    target against either mobs or players, and its periodic pulse (200009 -> 200008,
--    TARGET_UNIT_SRC_AREA_ENEMY) landed on nobody. UNIT_FLAG_NOT_SELECTABLE alone already makes
--    isTargetableForAttack() return false (Unit.cpp), so it's sufficient on its own to keep the
--    orb from being attacked - the two IMMUNE flags were both redundant for that purpose and
--    actively broke the orb's own damage. Removed, keeping NOT_SELECTABLE.
UPDATE `creature_template` SET `unit_flags` = 33554432 WHERE `entry` = 300001 AND `unit_flags` = 33555200;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- originally rev_1787763022007000003.sql
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Permafrost (200015) playtest bugfix, user-confirmed tuning (2026-08-26):
--
-- Live A/B test (7x Ice Lance at 5 stacks vs. 7x at 0 stacks) came back statistically identical
-- (125 vs 123 average damage) despite the damage-bonus code path tracing out correctly end to end.
-- Root cause: the stack buff's duration was only 3 sec (DurationIndex 27), a first-pass guess
-- flagged in mage_talents.csv's own notes as unconfirmed. Since a stack only refreshes while the
-- caster is actively moving, stopping to actually cast Ice Lance a few times let the whole bank
-- decay to 0 well before the 7-cast sample finished, diluting the bonus down to noise.
--
-- Bumped to 10 sec (DurationIndex 1, matches the existing stock 10000ms row - no new SpellDuration
-- row needed). Consumption also moved from spending 1 stack per Ice Lance cast to clearing the
-- entire bank in one cast, with the damage bonus now scaling per stack consumed (20% * stack
-- count) instead of a flat 20% regardless of banked count - see spell_mage.cpp
-- (spell_mage_ice_lance::ConsumePermafrost) and MageMechanics.cpp
-- (Mage::ApplyDoneDamagePctMods) for the accompanying code change.
UPDATE `spell_dbc` SET `DurationIndex` = 1 WHERE `ID` = 200015 AND `DurationIndex` = 27;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- originally rev_1787804681289117781.sql
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Icicles (200001) - root cause of "Frostbolt never gains Icicle stacks" (confirmed via live debug
-- logging: every cast successfully applied the aura, but always reported stack 1, never higher).
--
-- DurationIndex 0 does NOT mean "permanent" for SpellDuration.dbc specifically - unlike SpellCastTimes
-- /SpellRange/SpellRadius, the real client data has no row at all for SpellDuration ID 0, so
-- SpellInfo::GetDuration() (SpellInfo.cpp) falls through to a literal 0ms duration instead of -1.
-- Aura::CalcMaxDuration (SpellAuras.cpp) papers over this for PASSIVE auras only (forces -1 when
-- DurationEntry is null), which is why sibling rows like Biting Cold (200010-200012, also
-- DurationIndex 0) were unaffected - they're passive. Icicles isn't passive (it's a script-managed
-- stacking buff, not a known ability), so every recast synced to a fresh, already-expired 0-duration
-- aura instead of adding a stack to the one from the previous cast. Repointed to DurationIndex 21,
-- the real stock "permanent" row (Duration/MaxDuration both -1). See apps/dbc-tools/lib/reuse.py's
-- duration_index() for the matching pipeline-level fix so future spells don't hit this same bug.
UPDATE `spell_dbc` SET `DurationIndex` = 21 WHERE `ID` = 200001 AND `DurationIndex` = 0;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- originally rev_1787820084006262155.sql
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Root cause of "Evocation isn't restoring mana", found via live engine-level debug logging
-- (2026-08-26/27): Permafrost (12571) and Chilled to the Bone (44568) each have a SPELLMOD_EFFECT1
-- (-10 flat) modifier meant to scope only to Frostbolt/Cone of Cold (classmask 544), but that
-- modifier's classmask was landing empty at runtime - Player::ApplySpellMod's classmask check
-- (SpellInfo::IsAffected) treats an all-zero classmask as "matches every spell in the family"
-- (SpellInfo.cpp), so both mods were unconditionally applying -10/-10 to every mage spell's
-- EFFECT_0, including Evocation's mana-restore percentage (15% -> -5%, i.e. 0% after the engine's
-- own `std::max(amount, 0)` floor - AuraEffect::HandleObsModPowerAuraTick).
--
-- The actual bug: `spell_dbc`'s 9 EffectSpellClassMask{A,B,C}_{1,2,3} columns are physically
-- consumed in DECLARATION order (A_1,A_2,A_3,B_1,B_2,B_3,C_1,C_2,C_3 - confirmed against
-- data/sql/base/db_world/spell_dbc.sql's CREATE TABLE) and packed sequentially into the engine's
-- `std::array<flag96, 3> EffectSpellClassMask` (DBCStructure.h) - which is EFFECT-major, not
-- dword-major. That makes column "N" of letter-group X actually land in Effects[X-as-index]'s
-- dword N, not Effects[N-1]'s dword X as the "_1/_2/_3 = effect index" naming convention used by
-- every *other* per-effect field in this schema (EffectBasePoints_1/2/3, EffectAura_1/2/3, ...)
-- would suggest. Confirmed empirically: logging AuraEffect::CalculateSpellMod's actual computed
-- `mask` showed Effects[0]=(544,544,0) and Effects[1]=(0,0,0) for both rows, even though the
-- *_1/_2/_3-as-effect-index reading of the raw columns (EffectSpellClassMaskA_1=544/0,
-- EffectSpellClassMaskA_2=544 for both) looked like a normal, correctly-scoped pair.
--
-- This looks like a systemic mismatch, not something specific to these two rows - a search of
-- apps/dbc-tools/source/spells/mage_talents.csv alone turns up 60+ other "_2"/"_3"-suffixed
-- EffectSpellClassMask overrides (many on "pulled from existing data" rows, i.e. predating the
-- frost mage rework entirely), any of which could have the exact same transpose. NOT attempting a
-- blanket fix here - that needs a dedicated audit of the DBC build pipeline itself (whichever side
-- is "wrong": how the original bulk pull wrote these columns, or how dbcfmt.py documents them) and
-- is well out of scope for a live-playtest bugfix. This migration only corrects the rows actually
-- checked and confirmed to have the same broken pattern (EffectMiscValue_2=3,
-- EffectSpellClassMaskA_2=544, EffectSpellClassMaskB_1=0) - all 3 ranks of both Permafrost
-- (11175/12569/12571) and Chilled to the Bone (44566/44567/44568), not just the rank-3 capstones
-- that happened to be equipped on the test character that surfaced this. Moves each row's
-- Frostbolt|Cone of Cold classmask (544) off of the wrong column (EffectSpellClassMaskA_2, which
-- the engine reads as Effects[0]'s *second* dword) onto the column the engine actually reads as
-- Effects[1]'s first dword (EffectSpellClassMaskB_1).
UPDATE `spell_dbc` SET `EffectSpellClassMaskA_2` = 0, `EffectSpellClassMaskB_1` = 544
WHERE `ID` IN (11175, 12569, 12571, 44566, 44567, 44568)
  AND `EffectSpellClassMaskA_2` = 544 AND `EffectSpellClassMaskB_1` = 0;

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- originally rev_1787824212353499531.sql
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------
-- Conjure Refreshment's item (43518, Conjured Mana Pie): drop RequiredLevel from the real pulled
-- data's 74 to 1. The pulled RequiredLevel matched the old flat-value spell's level-gated tuning
-- (61828 "Refreshment" was learned at 75); now that Conjure Refreshment itself is learnable at 10
-- (see the mage.csv notes on 42955, docs/frost-mage-redesign.md sec 2) the item it conjures should
-- be usable immediately too, not gated 60+ levels above the spell that creates it. Plain UPDATE,
-- not DELETE+INSERT - item_template is on this repo's SQL linter's do-not-delete list (see the
-- Mana Agate/Mana Pie edits in rev_1787563173168071680.sql for the same reasoning). The
-- `RequiredLevel = 74` guard makes it a no-op on a second run.
UPDATE `item_template` SET `RequiredLevel` = 1 WHERE `entry` = 43518 AND `RequiredLevel` = 74;

